ROOT CAUSE
  AC-FSW4 asserted LIVE byte equality against another face's artifact, and AC-DIX3 compared
  the whole landed block byte for byte. Both quote a number that changes whenever the quoted
  face is re-rendered, which happens every closeout.

REPAIR (birth site, guards raised not lowered)
  AC-FSW4  existence + integer byte receipt (no live equality with others)
  AC-FSW9  new: the board must LABEL the bytes a snapshot, rendered from one constant
  AC-DIX15 new: newest band asserts the artifact NAME; bytes and stamp are labelled a snapshot
  AC-DIX16 new: board pages (face-sweep, ceo-blockers) never win the newest-artifact race
  AC-DIX7  now scored against the LANDED page, which is the half of AC-DIX3 that really
           caught a tampered ledger row - so dropping the byte-equality lost no protection
  suite    src/os/test_deliverable_index.py AC-DIX3 retargeted (verdict tamper must redden
           AC-DIX7) plus AC-DIX3b label-removal control; SUITE PASS 16/16 announced 16
  registry os-deliverable-index 14 -> 16 criteria, measured BY IMPORT: 690 suites / 5150

